From b5b3a65acbbe5c31c916dffedc1f0e7d93f9a1fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:48:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] control/controlhttp, feature/controlwebsocket: add opt-in
 WebSocket fallback for control

Some HTTP proxies intercept TLS and answer "Upgrade:
tailscale-control-protocol" with an ordinary HTTP response (a 403,
typically) but let WebSocket upgrades through, as in some sandboxes
for AI agents. feature/derpwebsocket lets a node behind such a proxy
reach DERP, but the node still can't reach the control server, so it
never logs in.

The control server already accepts the control protocol inside a
WebSocket for js/wasm clients. Add controlhttp.HookDialWebsocket,
called when the HTTP upgrade gets a non-101 response, and the opt-in
feature/controlwebsocket package that sets it: it dials the same URL
as a WebSocket with the Noise handshake initiation in the query
string, exactly as the js/wasm client does, reusing the failed
attempt's transport (dialer, proxy, TLS settings, HTTP/1.1 only).

Like derpwebsocket, neither tailscaled nor tsnet links it in. Without
the import, behavior is unchanged.

